# Copy to `.env` NEXT TO the compose file. Never commit the real thing.
#
#   install -m 600 /dev/null .env    # create it 0600 BEFORE writing secrets into it
#
# The secrets stay on the host on purpose. A secret routed through CI is a secret in that
# pipeline's logs, its cache, and the context of every pull request from a fork. CI ships an image;
# the host holds the credentials.
#
# THE PLACEHOLDERS BELOW CANNOT BOOT. `serve` refuses any secret beginning with `CHANGE_ME_` and
# names `openssl rand -base64 48` in the error, so copying this file into place and starting the
# stack fails loudly rather than running on a value published in a public repository. That is the
# whole reason the placeholders are spelled this way — see refusePlaceholders in
# cmd/tod-serve/serve.go, and TestServe_PlaceholderSecret_Refused, which reads THIS FILE and
# requires the values in it to be ones the binary rejects.
#
# TWO KINDS OF NAME LIVE HERE, and the prefix tells them apart:
#
#   TOD_DEPLOY_*   read by docker compose and by the deploy workflow. The binary never sees them.
#   TOD_*          read by the binary itself — every one of them is a constant in
#                  cmd/tod-serve/root.go, and gate ENV001 compares the two lists in both
#                  directions, so a variable invented here or forgotten there is a red build.
#
# Anything else (TRAEFIK_*) belongs to the proxy already running on the droplet.

# --- Deployment ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The DNS name Traefik routes to this service — and the SSH target the deploy workflow connects to,
# and the name DEPLOY_KNOWN_HOSTS must be keyscanned against. One record, one string.
TOD_DEPLOY_HOST=tod.example.com

# The image. The deploy workflow rewrites this line on every deploy with the exact image it
# shipped; leave it alone otherwise. compose.yaml has NO default for it, deliberately: a `.env`
# that lost this line must fail `docker compose config` rather than quietly upgrade to whatever a
# moving tag has become.
TOD_DEPLOY_IMAGE=ghcr.io/prokopto-dev/tod-serve:edge

# compose.local.yaml only — the host port it publishes. Unused by compose.yaml, which publishes
# nothing and is reached through Traefik.
TOD_DEPLOY_PORT=8080

# The external Docker network Traefik watches, and the names its static configuration gives its
# entrypoints and its certificate resolver. `docker network ls` if you are not sure.
#
# THESE NAMES ARE NOT STANDARD. Naming a certresolver that does not exist is silent: Traefik routes
# the host fine, never obtains a certificate, and serves its self-signed default — so every client
# sees a TLS error that points nowhere near the cause.
TRAEFIK_NETWORK=proxy
TRAEFIK_ENTRYPOINT_HTTP=http
TRAEFIK_ENTRYPOINT_HTTPS=https
TRAEFIK_CERTRESOLVER=http

# --- The two secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Generate each ONCE, with:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 48
#
# and keep them somewhere you will still have in a year. Both are effectively permanent.

# Keys every credential hash in the database — personal access tokens and browser sessions alike.
# It is what makes a stolen database FILE useless on its own, because the stored value is
# HMAC-SHA256(pepper, secret) and there is no way to re-derive it from the row.
#
# ROTATING IT INVALIDATES EVERY ISSUED TOKEN AND SIGNS EVERYBODY OUT. Every plugin destination then
# fails to report until its owner mints a new token. Treat it as permanent unless it has leaked.
TOD_TOKEN_PEPPER=CHANGE_ME_generate_with_openssl_rand_base64_48

# Signs every browser session cookie. Rotating it signs everybody out of the console and nothing
# else — no token is affected — so it is the less painful of the two to replace, but it is still a
# thing to generate once rather than under pressure.
TOD_SESSION_KEY=CHANGE_ME_generate_with_openssl_rand_base64_48

# --- Read by the binary, and set by the compose file rather than here -----------------------------
#
# Listed so that `TOD_*` here and the constants in cmd/tod-serve/root.go are the same set. Setting
# one of these in this file has no effect: the compose file names its own value.
#
# TOD_DB_PATH=/data/tod.db          a path INSIDE the container — a property of the image and the
#                                   volume, not a per-host preference
# TOD_ADDR=:8080                    likewise; EXPOSE, the Traefik loadbalancer port and the image's
#                                   HEALTHCHECK all name the same one
# TOD_PUBLIC_URL                    compose.yaml derives it from TOD_DEPLOY_HOST as
#                                   https://$TOD_DEPLOY_HOST. It must match the redirect URI
#                                   registered with the identity provider EXACTLY —
#                                   docs/operations/discord-app.md. compose.local.yaml lets you set
#                                   it, because at home there is no TOD_DEPLOY_HOST to derive from
# TOD_METRICS_ENABLED=false         a literal in the compose file. This stack publishes no port for
#                                   the metrics listener and gives Traefik no router for it, so
#                                   enabling it from here would bind something nothing can reach

# --- Read by the binary, optional, and off unless you set them ------------------------------------

# Where the OAuth callback sends a browser once it holds a ticket. Derived from TOD_PUBLIC_URL as
# `<public url>/join` when unset, which is right for every deployment that serves the console from
# this binary. Set it only if the console is served from somewhere else entirely.
# TOD_SPA_JOIN_URL=

# The metrics listener — canonical §13. It is a SECOND listener on its own address, and it is off
# unless TOD_METRICS_ENABLED is exactly `true`. Turning it on means editing the compose file, so
# that whatever is meant to reach it is decided in the same change; these two are here because they
# are what it needs once you do.
#
# TOD_METRICS_TOKEN is compared in constant time and is the only thing between a scrape endpoint
# and anybody who can reach the address. There is no default and no unauthenticated mode.
# TOD_METRICS_ADDR=:9090
# TOD_METRICS_TOKEN=
